(#4205).
- [designspaceLib] Fix ``DesignSpaceDocument.normalize()`` for mapped axes:
axis
  bounds and rule conditions are now normalized from their original values
(#4218).
- [designspaceLib] splitInterpolable and splitVariableFonts now warn when a
  source or instance is dropped because it lies outside the document's own
axes,
  instead of silently discarding it (#4244).
- [varLib.instancer] Add support for instancing variable COLRv1 fonts
(#2699, #4279).
- [varLib.instancer] Apply VVAR vertical-origin deltas to VORG, and use
OpenType
  rounding for instanced advances and vertical origins (#4221).
- [varLib.instancer] Keep a universal FeatureVariations record when pinning
removes
  its last condition but other axes remain (#4247).
- [varLib.instancer] Preserve ppem Device corrections in GDEF, BASE, GPOS
and JSTF
  instead of asserting on them (#4290).
- [varLib.instancer] Allow requesting an axis's original range on VARC
fonts (#4280).
- [varLib.instancer, subset] Fold, remove or remap MATH VariationIndex
devices
  when instancing, subsetting the GDEF store or optimizing it (#4288).
- [varLib] Raise ``ValueError: Missing required table fvar from
varLib.mutator``
  and the instancer CLI on a static font, instead of a bare KeyError
(#3751, #4300).
- [featureVars] When adding rvrn, also shift lookup indices inside existing
  FeatureVariations (#4233). Handle null ConditionSet and
  FeatureTableSubstitution offsets when building, subsetting and instancing
  (#4234, #4235). Keep FeatureTableSubstitution records sorted after
merging new
  ones into an existing record (#4248).
- [ttLib] Fix FeatureParams (size, ssXX, cvXX) in FeatureVariations
  alternate feature tables, which failed to compile and round-trip (#3623,
#4278).
- [ttLib] Fully decode lazily loaded ligatures, SinglePos and PairPos
arrays
  during recursive decompilation, so ``reorderGlyphs()`` on a lazy font no
longer
  corrupts or asserts on them (#4231, #4232).
- [VARC] Update the variation-store binary format to follow
  harfbuzz/boring-expansion-spec#175: ``SparseVarRegionList.RegionCount``
is uint32,
  sparse axes use Offset32 and MultiVarData items are stored in an INDEX.
VARC
  fonts built with earlier fontTools versions must be rebuilt (#4219).
- [VARC] Several fixes: derive component conditions from conditionIndex
(#4237),
  set the implicit scaleY when importing XML (#4238), report the font's
current
  coordinates for components that reset unspecified axes (#4239), and keep
inherited
  coordinates when drawing CFF2 VARC components (#4236).
- [varLib] buildMultiVarData accepts flattened per-region vector tuples
(#4245).
